    <node id="HEADQUARTERS">
      <data key="d0">HEADQUARTERS</data>
      <data key="d1">HEADQUARTERS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Headquarters is a historically significant old cabin, originally constructed by early backwoodsmen, situated in a remote area near a cane-brake. This rustic structure serves as a central gathering place for the local community, where social events, gambling, and storytelling are common activities. It is also the designated location where a jug is kept, likely for communal use during these gatherings. Beyond its role as a social hub, Headquarters is the site of a dramatic confrontation and physical fight between Don Carlo and a group of swindlers, marking it as a place of both communal tradition and intense personal conflict.
Relationships:
  - Source: BRINDLE BILL
  - Target: HEADQUARTERS
  - Description: Brindle Bill is a leading spirit at the headquarters, where he fills the jug and plays cards.
  - Source: DON CARLO
  - Target: HEADQUARTERS
  - Description: Don Carlo entered the headquarters cabin to confront the swindlers
  - Source: S. S. SIMON
  - Target: HEADQUARTERS
  - Description: S. S. Simon is seen heading to the headquarters with Brindle Bill and others.
  - Source: HEADQUARTERS
  - Target: SHIRT-TAIL BEND
  - Description: Headquarters is located in the locality of Shirt-tail Bend, near the river and cane-brake.
  - Source: DAN CARLO
  - Target: HEADQUARTERS
  - Description: Dan Carlo is seen heading to the headquarters with Brindle Bill and others, where he is expected to lose his money.
  - Source: SUNDOWN HILL
  - Target: HEADQUARTERS
  - Description: Sundown Hill is seen heading to the headquarters with the group.
  - Source: HEADQUARTERS
  - Target: SIMON'S WIFE
  - Description: Simon's wife set fire to the headquarters cabin to end the fight</data>
