    <node id="NUNNERY">
      <data key="d0">NUNNERY</data>
      <data key="d1">NUNNERY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The NUNNERY is a fortified, Portuguese-built structure located within the settlement, serving as the primary defensive stronghold for its occupants. It is the residence of Rudolph, who occupies a big, bare living-room and bedroom within the building—the very setting where a key scene involving Heywood and Peng takes place. Heywood identifies the nunnery as the best defensive position in the area, citing its strategic location, its access to a well (ensuring water supply), and its bell (likely used for signaling or alarms). During the conflict, the nunnery becomes the central refuge where the defenders are holed up, with its walls visibly pitted by gunfire, indicating it has come under direct attack. The structure combines residential and military functions, serving both as Rudolph’s home and as the last line of defense for the group.
Relationships:
  - Source: THE NUNNERY
  - Target: THE FIELD
  - Description: The nunnery is near the field where the white body is displayed, indicating proximity</data>
