    <node id="FIREPLACE">
      <data key="d0">FIREPLACE</data>
      <data key="d1">FIREPLACE</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">The fireplace is a central object located within the Deanery, serving as both a physical and symbolic focal point of the setting. It is the site where the Dean is often found standing, gazing into the flames, which underscores its role as a reflective and atmospheric element in the scene. Beyond its visual and emotional significance, the fireplace also anchors the spatial layout of the room, as it is the specific location that houses both the fire itself and an adjacent cupboard. This dual function—combining the warmth and light of the fire with the practical storage of the cupboard—makes the fireplace integral to the scene's composition, influencing both character positioning and narrative mood.
Relationships:
  - Source: CUPBOARD
  - Target: FIREPLACE
  - Description: The cupboard is near the fireplace.
  - Source: BRUIN
  - Target: FIREPLACE
  - Description: Bruin sits by the fireplace.
