    <node id="THE DUCHESS">
      <data key="d0">THE DUCHESS</data>
      <data key="d1">THE DUCHESS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The Duchess is a noblewoman and a member of the royal family, referenced alongside the King and Duke in the context of courtly society. She is specifically mentioned in Georgiana's comparison of her own comfort in a crowd, suggesting that the Duchess serves as a benchmark of social ease or public presence. Additionally, the Duchess attends the performance of the play "The Joviall Crew" at the Theatre, indicating her active participation in cultural and courtly events. Her role is that of a high-ranking female aristocrat, present in both royal and theatrical settings, and her mention in Georgiana's reflection highlights her as a figure of social comparison.
