    <node id="KING SLIGO">
      <data key="d0">KING SLIGO</data>
      <data key="d1">KING SLIGO</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">King Sligo is a wealthy and benevolent monarch who presides over a kingdom that includes a treasure chamber containing his riches. His wealth, however, becomes the target of theft, as his treasure is repeatedly stolen. In his time of need, King Sligo is aided by a coal—a seemingly humble but wise or magical object—that provides him with guidance. Following the coal’s instructions, King Sligo takes decisive action to catch the thief responsible for the thefts. He is portrayed as kind and just, relying on the coal’s counsel to protect his kingdom’s resources and restore order. His role as the owner of the treasure chamber places him at the center of the conflict, and his willingness to follow the coal’s advice demonstrates his trust in unconventional allies. Ultimately, King Sligo’s story revolves around his efforts to safeguard his wealth, his cooperation with the coal, and his successful pursuit of justice.
Relationships:
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: USEFUL COAL
  - Description: King Sligo spares the coal's life and follows its instructions to save his treasure
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: THE TREASURE-CHAMBER
  - Description: King Sligo keeps his treasure in the treasure-chamber and the key in his possession
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: TREASURE-CHAMBER
  - Description: King Sligo owns and guards the treasure chamber
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: COAL
  - Description: The coal advises and helps King Sligo catch the thief
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: HIGH CELLARER
  - Description: King Sligo trusts the High Cellarer and rewards him, unaware he is the thief
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: BLACK DIAMOND
  - Description: King Sligo places the coal in his crown, making it the Black Diamond
  - Source: KING SLIGO
  - Target: THE RUBY RING
  - Description: King Sligo gives the ruby ring to the High Cellarer as a reward</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
