      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Trelowarren is a location in Cornwall, England, encompassing both a wooded estate and a site of archaeological interest. As a wooded estate, it serves as the historic seat of the Vyvyan family, a prominent Cornish gentry family. The estate is notable for its extensive grounds and family heritage. Additionally, Trelowarren is recognized for its subterranean chambers and galleries, which extend approximately ninety feet in length. The origin of these underground structures remains unknown, though they are a significant feature of the site. The descriptions collectively portray Trelowarren as a place combining natural woodland, family history, and mysterious ancient underground architecture.
