    <node id="ORANGE TREES">
      <data key="d0">ORANGE TREES</data>
      <data key="d1">ORANGE TREES</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Orange trees are a notable feature of the courtyard and compound landscape, serving as a recurring backdrop for several key moments. In the courtyard, these trees provide a shaded pause point where Heywood and Rudolph stop during their interactions, grounding their conversation in a natural, tranquil setting. The same orange trees are also present in the broader compound, where they are associated with the early morning atmosphere: birds flutter among their branches, and this fluttering gradually ceases as the sun rises, marking a transition from night to day. Additionally, the trees are the site where a man disappears, with birds fluttering in the vicinity at that moment, adding an element of mystery or sudden change to the scene. Overall, the orange trees function as a consistent environmental element, linking moments of stillness, transition, and disappearance within the compound.

**Relationships:** None listed in the data.</data>
