    <node id="MULEY SULEIMAN">
      <data key="d0">MULEY SULEIMAN</data>
      <data key="d1">MULEY SULEIMAN</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Muley Suleiman was a Shereefian prince and the late Emperor of Morocco, belonging to the reigning dynasty and often referred to as "The Shereeff of Shereefs." He was a rigidly exact Mussulman who considered it indecent for Jewesses to disturb the frame of mind of pious Mussulmen. He was the uncle of Muley Abd Errahman, whom he nominated to the throne by a solemn dying request, preferring his nephew over his own children. Muley Suleiman died in 1822, having reigned for a quarter of a century. He was a good and patriotic prince who abolished Christian slavery. He also confirmed the treaty of 1801 in 1824 as Sultan of Morocco. He occasionally resided in Aghla.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
