      <data key="d0">OSMANLIS</data>
      <data key="d1">OSMANLIS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The Osmanlis, also known as the Turkish Sultans, are a dynastic line historically positioned as rivals to the Shereefian Sultans in the contest for the Caliphat (or Caliphate). Their claim to this supreme religious and political authority was considered less legitimate than that of the Shereefian line, which traced its descent from the Prophet Muhammad. Despite this perceived inferiority in legitimacy, the Osmanlis actively competed for the Caliphate, asserting their own authority and influence in the Islamic world. Their rivalry with the Shereefian Sultans was a significant feature of Islamic political history, with the Osmanlis representing a powerful, albeit contested, alternative claim to the spiritual and temporal leadership of the Muslim community.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.</data>
