    <node id="SAKI-PAN">
      <data key="d0">SAKI-PAN</data>
      <data key="d1">SAKI-PAN</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The Saki-Pan is a religious order or temple group, serving as the institutional body to which its priests belong. This order is referenced by the character Chop-Chin, who uses it to gain passage or access in a narrative context. The Saki-Pan is specifically associated with priests of the First Order, a rank or designation within the hierarchy. At the conclusion of the text, these priests are described as waking up, suggesting a ritual, ceremonial, or narrative event tied to their role. The order functions as a central authority or community for these priests, and its name is used as a credential or identifier in interactions. No contradictions exist in the provided descriptions, which together establish the Saki-Pan as a formal religious institution with a defined priestly class, active in the story's events.
Relationships:
  - (No relationships listed in the provided data)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
