      <data key="d3">EXCELSIOR BANK is a financial institution located in San Francisco. It is notably managed by Trixit, a firm that also oversees other banking operations. The bank’s suspension of operations was a contributing factor to the broader financial crisis, indicating its significant role in the regional economy at the time. Additionally, the bank is led by a president named Johnson, who serves as its chief executive. Combining these details, Excelsior Bank is a San Francisco-based institution under Trixit’s management, with Johnson as its president, and its suspension played a part in the financial turmoil.
