    <node id="THE GANG">
      <data key="d0">THE GANG</data>
      <data key="d1">THE GANG</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The Gang is a criminal organization operating in and around the city and the surrounding valley and canyon areas. The group is primarily known as a band of counterfeiters, producing and selling bad money to unsuspecting customers. One of its members is Snipes, who is directly involved in the counterfeiting operations. In addition to counterfeiting, the gang also engages in highway robbery, most notably the stagecoach robbery, which leads to a subsequent search for the stolen money.

The gang is led by a figure known as Snapshot Harry, who is also referred to as Uncle Harry in some contexts. Under his leadership, the group is involved in the robbery of a coach, but internal betrayal occurs, as some members turn against Harry. Despite this, the gang, still under Harry's direction, is also involved in the recovery of the stolen money, operating primarily in the canyon area.

The gang is composed of men in the valley who are associated with Uncle Harry. These men may be suspicious of Brice, a character who, along with Flora, keeps secrets from the group. The gang's activities and internal dynamics are central to the narrative, with Brice and Flora withholding information from them.

Additionally, the gang has a former member named Rags, who has left the group, as mentioned in the final paragraph of the source material. The gang's operations are thus multifaceted, involving both counterfeiting and violent robbery, and are marked by internal conflict and betrayal, all while being led by the charismatic but ultimately betrayed Snapshot Harry/Uncle Harry.
Relationships: None listed</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
