      <data key="d3">Miss Webb is a medical professional who works alongside a colleague named Elsie, with whom she is involved in the treatment and care of patients. In addition to her clinical duties, Miss Webb is a committed advocate for women’s suffrage, described as a “great franchise woman.” She actively supports the franchise movement—the campaign for women’s right to vote—and is associated with a local women’s organization, referred to as her L.W.A. (likely a local women’s association). However, her involvement with this association has presented certain difficulties, though the specific nature of these challenges is not detailed. Miss Webb’s dual role as a healthcare worker and a suffrage supporter highlights her engagement both in her profession and in the broader social and political movements of her time.
