      <data key="d3">Pearls are precious gems that appear in the narrative as objects of significant value and beauty. They are notably worn by the gorgeous wives of the merchants, serving as symbols of wealth, status, and adornment. In addition to their role as decorative jewelry, pearls hold a magical or supernatural quality in the story: they are one of two types of precious objects that fall from Eily's mouth whenever she speaks, the other being diamonds. This unique phenomenon ties pearls directly to Eily's character, marking her speech as a source of extraordinary fortune. Thus, pearls function both as tangible luxury items in the merchant world and as magical byproducts of Eily's voice, bridging the realms of material wealth and enchanted occurrence.
