    <node id="ATLAS">
      <data key="d0">ATLAS</data>
      <data key="d1">ATLAS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The ATLAS mountain range, commonly referred to as the Atlas, is a significant geographical feature that begins at the frontiers of ALGERIA and extends outward to Cape Gheer. This range marks a clear geographical boundary, originating from the Algerian border and stretching in a continuous line to its terminal point at Cape Gheer. The Atlas serves as a natural demarcation, with its eastern or southern limits anchored at Algeria's frontier, from which it proceeds westward or northward toward the coastal cape. The descriptions consistently affirm that the range's starting reference is the Algerian border, and its full extent culminates at Cape Gheer, providing a definitive span for this mountain system. No contradictions exist between the provided statements; both emphasize the same origin and endpoint, with the second description explicitly noting the boundary function of the range. Thus, the Atlas is a mountain range that begins at Algeria's frontier and extends to Cape Gheer, acting as a geographical boundary in the region. 
