      <data key="d1">THE COWS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">The cows are livestock residing on a farm, where they are kept in the stalls of the barn. They are depicted as peaceful, contented animals that munch on their feed while gazing at the human fighters present, offering a stark contrast to the violence occurring around them. As part of the farm's rural setting, the cows symbolize the tranquil, pastoral life that the farmer offers to Snipes, highlighting the peaceful alternative to conflict.
Relationships:
  - Source: THE BARN
  - Target: THE COWS
  - Description: The cows are in the stalls of the barn, being part of the environment where the fight occurs.
  - Source: THE PRINCIPALS
  - Target: THE COWS
  - Description: The cows gaze at the principals with curiosity, showing a passive observation of the fighters.
  - Source: THE FARMER
  - Target: THE COWS
  - Description: The cows are part of the farmer's farm, mentioned as part of the rural life he offers</data>
