      <data key="d6">ENTITY: BATTLE OF PITTSBURG LANDING
Description: The Battle of Pittsburg Landing, also known as the Battle of Shiloh, was a major engagement of the American Civil War, fought near Pittsburg Landing, Tennessee. This two-day battle pitted Union forces against Confederate forces and is notable for its intensity and high casualties. On the second day of the battle, Captain Acker was killed in action. The battle is historically significant as one of the bloodiest early conflicts of the war, marking a turning point in the Western Theater.
