    <node id="PITTSBURG LANDING">
      <data key="d0">PITTSBURG LANDING</data>
      <data key="d1">PITTSBURG LANDING</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">PITTSBURG LANDING is a significant historical site located on the Tennessee River in Tennessee. It is most notably recognized as the location of a major battle in April 1862, commonly known as the Battle of Shiloh. This landing served as the Union's base and the site where Union forces were encamped prior to and during the engagement. It was at Pittsburg Landing that General Buell arrived with reinforcements to support General Grant's troops, a crucial moment in the battle. The First Minnesota Battery also fought at this location during the conflict. Thus, Pittsburg Landing is synonymous with the Battle of Shiloh, serving as both the geographical setting and the Union's strategic staging ground.
Relationships:
  - Source: BATTLE OF PITTSBURG LANDING
  - Target: PITTSBURG LANDING
  - Description: The battle took place at Pittsburg Landing
  - Source: PITTSBURG LANDING
  - Target: BATTLE OF PITTSBURG LANDING
  - Description: Pittsburg Landing is the site of the Battle of Pittsburg Landing
  - Source: PITTSBURG LANDING
  - Target: SHILOH
  - Description: Pittsburg Landing is the same location as Shiloh</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
