    <node id="ST HILAIRE">
      <data key="d0">ST HILAIRE</data>
      <data key="d1">ST HILAIRE</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">ST HILAIRE was a strategically significant location during the rebellion, situated approximately seven miles from St Charles. It was near this site that Brown conducted a reconnaissance mission and subsequently destroyed a bridge as part of military operations. Additionally, St Hilaire served as a point where Wetherall obtained crucial intelligence, though a reinforcement column arrived there too late to alter the course of events. The location thus played a dual role in the conflict: as a site of tactical destruction by Brown and as a gathering point for delayed reinforcements under Wetherall.
Relationships: (None listed in the relationships table)</data>
