**ENTITY: THE WILL**
Description: The will is a legal document that serves as the last testament of the narrator's uncle, formally examined and proved in front of Dr. Williams and Tom Trice. It is a document that people are greedy to see, though they are not asked to view it until the following day. The will was dictated by Young Simon, who bequeathed all his possessions to Roxie Daymon, a decision that cousin Cæsar seeks to contest. The document is read and discussed by the narrator and relatives, with three witnesses present, all of whom are legatees. The reading takes place at Mr. Rawlinson's, where the distribution of the narrator's family's assets is outlined, leading to subsequent discussions among relatives. The will is central to the family's legal and emotional dynamics, as it determines the inheritance and sparks conflict over its provisions.
Relationships: None listed in the provided data.

