      <data key="d3">AROERIS is a figure from Egyptian mythology, identified as the brother of Osiris, and also of Isis and Typho (often associated with Set). He is notably characterized as a peace-maker among these deities, playing a role in mediating or reconciling conflicts within the divine family. While his primary familial connection is to Osiris, his broader sibling relationship with Isis and Typho places him within the central mythological narrative of the Osiris cycle. His role as a peace-maker suggests a stabilizing or harmonizing influence, contrasting with the more turbulent dynamics often associated with Typho/Set. Thus, AROERIS is a divine sibling and conciliatory figure within the Egyptian pantheon.

