    <edge source="GRANDMOTHER" target="WOODCHUCK" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">GRANDMOTHER</data>
      <data key="d8">WOODCHUCK</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">GRANDMOTHER and WOODCHUCK share a warm, if not deeply intimate, friendship. The grandmother acknowledges the woodchucks visit and trusts that he enjoyed his time with her. Their bond is one of mutual respect and affection, though it is not as close as a familial or very tight-knit relationship. Demonstrating her care, the grandmother knits a red-worsted cover for the woodchuck and, after his visit, places him in the cupboardan act that suggests she values his comfort and well-being, treating him with gentle hospitality. Together, these actions paint a picture of a kind, nurturing grandmother who welcomes the woodchuck as a friend, and a woodchuck who is a welcomed guest in her home.</data>
      <data key="d12">GRANDMOTHER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GRANDMOTHER" target="HEARTH" id="related_to">
