    <edge source="MAYAS" target="CHAACMOL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MAYAS</data>
      <data key="d8">CHAACMOL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Chaacmol is a significant figure directly linked to the Maya civilization, specifically originating from the region of Mayab. He is identified as a Maya warrior and chieftain, whose legacy is preserved through a statue that reflects key aspects of Maya customs and traditions. The statue of Chaacmol is closely associated with funeral sacrifices, indicating that it held ritual importance in Maya burial practices. Additionally, the statue is depicted with a band of cloth on its head, a distinctive feature that further ties it to Maya cultural iconography. Chaacmol's mausoleum, which houses this statue, is said to reflect Maya customs, reinforcing his role as a prominent leader whose burial site served as a testament to Maya beliefs and funerary rites. Overall, Chaacmol stands as a warrior, chieftain, and cultural symbol, with his statue and mausoleum serving as enduring representations of Maya heritage and ceremonial life.</data>
      <data key="d12">CHAACMOL</data>
    </edge>
