      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Lizard folk avoid Pistol Meadow after dark due to a superstition regarding ghosts. This belief is consistently noted in the available descriptions, with no contradictory information provided. The superstition appears to be a cultural or traditional taboo among the lizard folk, leading them to steer clear of the meadow during nighttime hours. The exact nature of the ghost-related belief is not elaborated upon, but it is sufficient to deter the lizard folk from entering the area after sunset. Pistol Meadow itself is the specific location avoided, and the lizard folk are the group that holds this superstition. No other details about the meadow, the lizard folk's broader customs, or the origin of the ghost story are given. The avoidance is thus a clear, singular behavioral pattern tied to supernatural fear.</data>
      <data key="d12">LIZARD FOLK</data>
    </edge>
