    <edge source="EXCALIBUR" target="DOZMARE POOL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">EXCALIBUR</data>
      <data key="d8">DOZMARE POOL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">EXCALIBUR, the legendary sword of King Arthur, was cast into DOZMARE POOL, a body of water in Cornwall, England, by Sir Bedevere. This act is a pivotal moment in Arthurian legend, occurring after King Arthurs final battle against his treacherous nephew Mordred. According to the accounts, the wounded Arthur, knowing his end was near, instructed Sir Bedevere to take the sword and throw it into the lake. Bedevere, initially reluctant to part with such a powerful relic, twice hid the sword and claimed he had disposed of it, but Arthur saw through his deception. On the third attempt, Bedevere truly threw Excalibur into the water. As the sword arced through the air, a hand and arm rose from the surface of the pool, caught the blade, and drew it beneath the water, never to be seen again. This event is described in the text as occurring at Dozmare Pool, which is explicitly identified as the "mere" (a term for a lake or pool) referenced in the original Arthurian narratives. The identification of Dozmare Pool as the exact location is significant, as it grounds the myth in a real geographic site in Cornwall. The pool, a remote and dark tarn, has since become a place of local legend and tourism, associated with the enduring story of Arthurs final moments and the return of his sword to the Lady of the Lake. The act of throwing Excalibur into the water symbolizes the end of Arthurs reign and the passing of the magical age, as the sword was not merely a weapon but a symbol of sovereignty and divine right. Sir Bedeveres role as the one who carried out this final command underscores his loyalty and the solemnity of the moment. Thus, the combined descriptions confirm that Excalibur was deliberately and irrevocably returned to the waters of Dozmare Pool, marking the conclusion of King Arthurs story and the beginning of his legends enduring legacy.</data>
      <data key="d12">DOZMARE POOL</data>
    </edge>
