      <data key="d12">YGRAYNE</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YGRAYNE" target="DUKE OF CORNWALL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">YGRAYNE</data>
      <data key="d8">DUKE OF CORNWALL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Ygrayne was the wife of the Duke of Cornwall before marrying Uther Pendragon</data>
      <data key="d12">DUKE OF CORNWALL</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="YGRAYNE" target="UTHER PENDRAGON" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">YGRAYNE</data>
      <data key="d8">UTHER PENDRAGON</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Ygrayne, also known as Igraine in some traditions, is a central figure in Arthurian legend. She was originally married to Gorlois, the Duke of Cornwall, with whom she had daughters, including Morgause and Elaine. After Gorlois was slain in battle, Ygrayne married Uther Pendragon, the King of Britain. This marriage was significant because it legitimized Uther's rule and set the stage for the birth of their son, Arthur, who would later become the legendary King of the Britons. Ygrayne's union with Uther was orchestrated under dramatic circumstances, often involving magic and prophecy, and her role as Arthur's mother is pivotal to the overarching narrative of the Arthurian cycle. Her story intertwines themes of loyalty, political alliance, and destiny, marking her as a key maternal and royal figure in the legends surrounding Camelot.</data>
      <data key="d12">YGRAYNE</data>
    </edge>
