    <edge source="TINKA" target="THE PAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">TINKA</data>
      <data key="d8">THE PAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Tinka, a character associated with the magical object known as "The Pan," uses this enchanted item in a dual and somewhat contradictory manner. Initially, Tinka salted the pan with golda deceptive act designed to trick Jack Fleming into returning, by making it appear that the pan had found real gold. However, this same pan is later used by Tinka for a legitimate purpose: to help Fleming with actual gold panning. The pan thus serves both as a tool of deception and as a genuine aid in the search for gold. Tinkas actions with the pan are central to her interactions with Fleming, blending trickery with practical assistance. Ultimately, the pan is a versatile instrument in Tinkas hands, capable of both misleading and supporting, and it plays a key role in her relationship with Fleming.</data>
      <data key="d12">TINKA</data>
    </edge>
