      <data key="d8">FRENCH</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Mogador, a city on the Atlantic coast of Morocco, was the site of a significant military action by French forces in August 1844. During this bombardment, the French navy targeted the city, causing widespread destruction. The attack was so severe that it led to the subsequent plundering of Mogador, as the chaos and damage left the city vulnerable to looting. This event was part of a broader conflict between France and Morocco, reflecting the tensions of the era. The bombardment and its aftermath had a lasting impact on the city, marking a violent episode in its history.</data>
      <data key="d12">FRENCH</data>
    </edge>
