    <edge source="HERCULES" target="DEIANIRA" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">HERCULES</data>
      <data key="d8">DEIANIRA</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Hercules, also known as Heracles in Greek mythology, is a legendary hero renowned for his immense strength and numerous heroic feats. Among his many relationships, Hercules loved and eventually married Deianira, a princess of Calydon. Their union, however, was not without conflict: Hercules love for Deianira directly led to a fierce struggle with the river god Achelous, who was also a suitor for her hand. Hercules defeated Achelous in this contest, securing Deianira as his wife. As his spouse, Deianira became central to Hercules later life, though their story ultimately ended in tragedy, as a misunderstanding involving a poisoned garment she gave him led to his demise. Together, Hercules and Deianira are a key couple in Greek myth, bound by love, rivalry, and fate.</data>
      <data key="d12">DEIANIRA</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HERCULES" target="ACHELOUS" id="related_to">
