    <edge source="EAGLE INN" target="PHILADELPHIA GAME MARKET" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">EAGLE INN</data>
      <data key="d8">PHILADELPHIA GAME MARKET</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Eagle Inn is known as a headquarters for pothunters from the Philadelphia game market.</data>
      <data key="d12">EAGLE INN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HADE" target="THE FIGHT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">HADE</data>
      <data key="d8">THE FIGHT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">HADE is a character who finds himself at a violent event known as "THE FIGHT," despite his deep-seated fear. His presence at the fight is not voluntary; he is compelled to attend due to a difficult situation involving a figure named Keppler, which forces him into this dangerous environment against his will. Once at the fight, Hade acts as a spectator, observing the proceedings rather than participating. However, when law enforcement stages a raid on the event, Hade attempts to flee the scene, seeking to escape the chaos and avoid the consequences of being caught there. His actions reveal a man caught between external pressure and personal survival, ultimately prioritizing his own safety when the situation escalates.</data>
      <data key="d12">THE FIGHT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HADE" target="EAGLE INN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">HADE</data>
      <data key="d8">EAGLE INN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The stranger, suspected to be Hade, enters the Eagle Inn, linking him to the location.</data>
      <data key="d12">EAGLE INN</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="KEPPLER" target="THE FIGHT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">KEPPLER</data>
      <data key="d8">THE FIGHT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Keppler is a central figure in the organization and execution of the event known as "The Fight." He possesses inside knowledge of the contest, which he uses to assist in its preparation, ensuring that all logistical and strategic elements are in place. In addition to his preparatory role, Keppler serves as the master of ceremonies during the event itself. In this capacity, he commands the fighters, giving them direction, and also attempts to manage and control the crowd, maintaining order and guiding the atmosphere of the proceedings. Thus, Keppler is both a behind-the-scenes organizer and a public-facing authority figure for The Fight.</data>
      <data key="d12">THE FIGHT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HEFFLEFINGER" target="THE FIGHT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">HEFFLEFINGER</data>
      <data key="d8">THE FIGHT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Hefflefinger is at the fight to capture Hade, making the event central to his mission.</data>
      <data key="d12">THE FIGHT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICHAEL E. DWYER" target="THE FIGHT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MICHAEL E. DWYER</data>
      <data key="d8">THE FIGHT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Dwyer plans to attend the fight to point out Hade to the detective.</data>
      <data key="d12">THE FIGHT</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DWYER" target="THE FIGHT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">DWYER</data>
      <data key="d8">THE FIGHT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Dwyer is an individual present at the event known as "The Fight," where he serves as a spectator. He is positioned near Hade, which places him in close proximity to the action and suggests his active involvement in the proceedings. Throughout the fight, Dwyer reacts to the unfolding events, notably nodding in agreement with a correspondent who is also covering or observing the match. His physical presence at the scene, combined with his attentive and responsive behavior, indicates that he is engaged with the fight, both as an onlooker and as someone who aligns with the correspondent's perspective on the events. Dwyer's role is that of a participatory observer, contributing to the atmosphere of the event through his reactions and his proximity to key figures like Hade.</data>
      <data key="d12">THE FIGHT</data>
    </edge>
